.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH loom-vault 1  "loom-vault " 
.SH NAME
loom\-vault \- Vault commands (RPC). Only `add` may prompt
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBloom\-vault\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Vault commands (RPC). Only `add` may prompt
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
loom\-vault\-grant(1)
`loom vault grant` arguments
.TP
loom\-vault\-revoke(1)
`loom vault revoke` arguments
.TP
loom\-vault\-list(1)
`loom vault list` arguments
.TP
loom\-vault\-add(1)
`loom vault add <provider>` arguments. Two flows:
.TP
loom\-vault\-delete(1)
`vault delete <label> [\-\-force]` — remove a credential. Cascade revokes active grants when `\-\-force` is set; otherwise blocks with `credential_in_use` if any grant references the label
.TP
loom\-vault\-list\-labels(1)
`vault list\-labels` — enumerate stored credential labels. Distinct from `vault list` which lists *grants*
.TP
loom\-vault\-diagnose(1)
`vault diagnose` — backend status + last\-error snapshot. Output is a stable JSON schema (A\-W6.4) for `jq` automation
.TP
loom\-vault\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
